<title>USA: Celgene seeks thalidomide approval for HIV. [CORRECTED 00:16 GMT 30/1]</title>
<headline>Celgene seeks thalidomide approval for HIV. [CORRECTED 00:16 GMT 30/1]</headline>
<dateline>WARREN, N.J. 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Celgene Corp on Wednesday said it would file a new drug application for the use of thalidomide to treat wasting in HIV patients.</p>
<p>&quot;Preliminary review of the data appears very positive, showing statistically significant weight gain,&quot; said John Jackson, chairman and chief executive officer, in a statement about the company's Phase II/III (corrects from Phase I/II) trials of the drug.</p>
</text>
